===Climate===
[[File:Hirogawa Iwashi Fleet.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The iwashi fishing fleet returning to Hirogawa harbor during the autumn sardine run.]]

Hirogawa Prefecture experiences a humid subtropical climate (Köppen classification Cfa) moderated by the warm currents of the Sea of Mitoyagi. The strait's maritime influence ensures mild winters and warm, humid summers with consistent rainfall throughout the year. The prefecture's position at the mouth of the strait creates distinctive wind patterns, with strong seasonal currents driving the iwashi runs that define the regional economy.

The autumn months bring the celebrated {{nihongo|'''Iwashi Season'''|鰯の季節|Iwashi no Kisetsu}}, when cooling ocean temperatures drive massive schools of sardines through the Hirogawa Strait—a natural phenomenon that has shaped the region's economy, cuisine, and cultural identity for centuries.

As illustrated by the climate data for the capital city below, the region is characterized by warm, stable temperatures year-round with high humidity and significant precipitation. The maritime influence is evident in the minimal seasonal temperature variation compared to inland prefectures.

